1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 b6 4. e4 Bb4 5. Bd3 Bb7 6. Qc2 Nc6 7. Nge2 e5 8. Be3
exd4 9. Nxd4 Ne5 10. f3 Ba6 11. b3 d5 12. exd5 Nxd5 13. cxd5 Nxd3+ 14. Kd2 O-O
15. Nc6 Qd6 16. Nxb4 Qxb4 17. a3 Qd6 18. Kd1 Qe5 19. Rb1 Qxe3 {Reid was
tournament organiser and had had to play himself due to foreign players
dropping out. The game was scheduled to be played in the first round, 22 May,
but reports indicate that Thomas played two other games, in advance of the
schedule, on that day. Can Thomas have played three games in one day? I am
wondering whether this game might have been played off on the following day,
Sunday 23 May, when no other games were scheduled. JS} 0-1

