28. Bd5+ Kh8 29. f6 Bxf6 30. gxf6 Rd7 31. Bh6 Ne6 32. Bg7+ {Source: BCM, July
1926, p314. N.b. White's name given as Hon. AL Lowther in this score but it
appears as Hon. AJ Lowther in most chess references. His full name was Arthur
James Beresford Lowther (1888-1967), son of the 1st Viscount Ullswater,
speaker of the House of Commons during WW1, hence the Hon. He served during
the war, became a barrister and colonial administrator.} 1-0

