21. Qxd6 {Source: Sussex Daily News of 4.6.1926. Both the Scarborough Evening
News and Daily Post of 27.5.1926 and the Scarborough Standard and North and
East Ridings Gazette state that there were 28 boards in the simultaneous,
while the British Chess Magazine of July 1926 indicates that 29 games were
played. The Scarborough newspapers also give the date for the display as 26th
May while the BCM gives the date as 28th May. Also published in the Big
Database 2021, which indicates that the game was played on 28th May as part of
a 35 board simul (Brian Denman Collection)} 1-0

